1. Algorithmic approach to find solution to problems that involve many possible paths
2. here solutions are build step by step
3. it is a controled recursion (here we abondon paths if it does not return solution)

How Back tracking work:
    1. Explore one option
    2. keep building the solution with recursion
        1. if violates conditions back track and explore new paths
        2. if valid solution return it

In back tracking we make changes in place :
        a,b,c  -> c,b,a -> b,c,a -> b,a,c (just swaping)